cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, or the verification results it documents, please cite it as below."
title: "Polymer Analysis Toolkit: characterisation analysis that states its own limits"
abstract: >-
  PAT is an open-source web application that computes molecular, thermal,
  mechanical, rheological and structural properties of polymers from data
  laboratories already produce (GPC/SEC, DSC, TGA, tensile, rheology, XRD,
  FTIR). This record documents what the tool computes, how each result was
  verified against published values, and — in more detail than is customary —
  what could not be verified. Verification ran against a certified reference,
  three open Zenodo datasets and four raw figshare datasets from a single
  laboratory. The central finding is a failure pattern rather than an
  arithmetic error: in every module tested the analysis accepted an input that
  was not physically what the code assumed — a transmittance spectrum where
  absorbance was expected, a heat-flow trace whose endotherm pointed down, a
  thermogravimetric trace ending at negative mass — and returned a confident
  number instead of refusing. These defects were invisible to internally
  consistent synthetic tests. The limits that remain unresolved are recorded in
  the test suite as strict xfails, so that an unexpected pass fails the build.
